// DECLARED 2026-10-01 for a withdrawal made 2026-09-19 and recorded until now only as an annotation
// (v2.workflow.required_floor, THE NOMINAL ROSTER). The operator cut `v2.test.` from
// required_gate_prefixes on preparation cost, and a lowered rung that exists only as a `//` comment
// cannot be read by anything (DESIGN section 4b(3)), so the v2 suite's claims went silently red on main:
// adhoc-095d4a35-c40 found two in reference_conservation by accident (gunbc#12812, gunbc#12845). The
// population below is MEASURED, not estimated: neat-boar-16's srv1 probe ran the restored family at
// eff2d73b14, and every red identity it observed is named here with its owner. The family's
// cost is the reason it stays out: a prefix is a preparation SEED, so every pull request prepares the
// whole family whatever it changed (the probe: about 3,569 modules resolved and 3,096 s wall, against
// about 101 s of claim evaluation), the same shape the 2026-09-19 receipt measured.

